.TH TTY 1 "2026" "spicule" "spicule User Commands"
.SH NAME
tty \- return the terminal name of standard input
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tty
.RB [ \-s ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tty
writes to standard output the name of the terminal open as standard
input, using the same name
.BR ttyname (3)
would return for that descriptor. If standard input is not a
terminal, the line
"\fBnot a tty\fR"
is written instead.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-s
Silent: suppress the name (or
"\fBnot a tty\fR" )
line entirely; report the result only through the exit status. This
option was removed from the POSIX specification as of Issue 6, but is
implemented here as the widely supported extension every common
.BR tty (1)
still carries forward from the earlier standard.
.SH OPERANDS
None.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Standard input is a terminal.
.TP
.B 1
Standard input is not a terminal.
.TP
.B >1
An error occurred: an invalid option, a write failure, or a failure
determining whether standard input is a terminal for a reason other
than it simply not being one.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mesg (1),
.BR write (1),
.BR stty (1)
